Subject: [PATCH] clk: bcm: rpi: Export the H.264 firmware clock

The firmware lists the H.264 block's clock (id 6) in GET_CLOCKS, but the
driver has no variant for it, so it is never registered and no consumer can
request it. Register it like the ISP and HEVC clocks (minimise, critical).

Measured on a Pi 4 (6.18.50+rpt): with the default ondemand governor the
firmware runs the H.264 block at 250 MHz during V4L2 decode (the ARM never
reaches turbo), giving 53-54 fps for a 1080p H.264 stream; with the block at
500-650 MHz the same stream decodes at 90-97 fps.

---
--- a/drivers/clk/bcm/clk-raspberrypi.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/bcm/clk-raspberrypi.c
@@ -149,6 +149,11 @@
 		.minimize = true,
 		.flags = CLK_IS_CRITICAL,
 	},
+	[RPI_FIRMWARE_H264_CLK_ID] = {
+		.export = true,
+		.minimize = true,
+		.flags = CLK_IS_CRITICAL,
+	},
 	[RPI_FIRMWARE_ISP_CLK_ID] = {
 		.export = true,
 		.minimize = true,
